problem:
Problem description
- There is a finite planning horizon of $$T$$ yearly decision periods, indexed by $$t\in\mathcal T=\{1,\ldots,T\}$$.
- There are $$P$$ investment products, indexed by $$p\in\mathcal P=\{1,\ldots,P\}$$.
- The planner starts with initial liquid capital $$C_0$$ at the beginning of period $$1$$.
- Each product $$p$$ has a set of periods when it can be purchased, a fixed gross payout multiplier at maturity, a maturity delay measured in periods, and a maximum investable amount.
- At the beginning of each period, only the cash currently on hand may be allocated. Cash on hand includes the initial capital and any proceeds from investments that have already matured.
- No borrowing, leverage, or negative cash positions are allowed.
- A product may only receive investment in periods when it is available.
- Investments in each product must respect its capacity; a product with unlimited capacity may accept any nonnegative amount of available cash.
- Cash that is not invested in a period remains liquid and may be used in later periods.
- Proceeds are received at the specified maturity time and become part of the cash available at the appropriate later decision time.
- The planning goal is to choose the investment amounts so that the total wealth at the end of period $$T$$ is maximized.
- A solution is represented by:
  - $$x_{p,t}$$: the amount invested in product $$p$$ at the beginning of period $$t$$.
  - $$b_t$$: the liquid cash available at the beginning of period $$t$$.
  - $$W_T$$: the total wealth at the end of period $$T$$.

Input Format
{
  "time_horizon": {
    "symbol": "$$T$$",
    "type": "$$\\mathbb{Z}_{>0}$$",
    "meaning": "number of yearly decision periods"
  },
  "initial_capital": {
    "symbol": "$$C_0$$",
    "type": "$$\\mathbb{R}_{\\ge 0}$$",
    "meaning": "cash available at the beginning of period $$1$$"
  },
  "products": {
    "symbol": "$$\\mathcal P$$",
    "type": "array of length $$P$$",
    "meaning": "investment products"
  },
  "product_fields": {
    "available_periods": {
      "symbol": "$$\\mathcal A_p\\subseteq\\mathcal T$$",
      "type": "list of integers",
      "meaning": "periods when product $$p$$ can be purchased"
    },
    "maturity_delay": {
      "symbol": "$$d_p$$",
      "type": "$$\\mathbb{Z}_{\\ge 0}$$",
      "meaning": "number of periods from purchase to payout"
    },
    "gross_multiplier": {
      "symbol": "$$\\alpha_p$$",
      "type": "$$\\mathbb{R}_{\\ge 0}$$",
      "meaning": "cash received per unit invested at maturity"
    },
    "capacity": {
      "symbol": "$$U_p$$",
      "type": "$$\\mathbb{R}_{\\ge 0}\\cup\\{+\\infty\\}$$",
      "meaning": "maximum amount that may be invested in product $$p$$ in one purchase period"
    }
  },
  "planning_goal": {
    "symbol": "$$\\max W_T$$",
    "meaning": "maximize total wealth at the end of period $$T$$"
  }
}

Output Format
{
  "investment_plan": {
    "symbol": "$$X=[x_{p,t}]$$",
    "shape": "$$P\\times T$$",
    "meaning": "investment amount in each product $$p$$ at each period $$t$$"
  },
  "cash_balance": {
    "symbol": "$$b_t$$",
    "shape": "$$T+1$$",
    "meaning": "liquid cash available at each decision time, including the initial time and the final time"
  },
  "terminal_wealth": {
    "symbol": "$$W_T$$",
    "shape": "scalar",
    "meaning": "total wealth at the end of period $$T$$"
  }
}

Example(s)

Input 1
{
  "time_horizon": 3,
  "initial_capital": 500000,
  "products": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "available_periods": [1, 2, 3],
      "maturity_delay": 0,
      "gross_multiplier": 1.20,
      "capacity": "unlimited"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "available_periods": [1],
      "maturity_delay": 1,
      "gross_multiplier": 1.50,
      "capacity": 120000
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "available_periods": [2],
      "maturity_delay": 0,
      "gross_multiplier": 1.60,
      "capacity": 150000
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "available_periods": [3],
      "maturity_delay": 0,
      "gross_multiplier": 1.40,
      "capacity": 100000
    }
  ]
}
